      "description": "Watch Rio Ave vs FC Porto highlights and goals from Primeira Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The Primeira Liga spotlight turned to Vila do Conde on August 15, 2026, as Rio Ave hosted FC Porto in a highly anticipated early-season fixture. Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish their dominance in a match that promised tactical intrigue from the opening whistle. Early Dominance and VAR Drama FC Porto wasted little time making their presence felt. In the 11th minute, the visitors capitalized on a set-piece opportunity when Gabriel Veiga swung in a dangerous corner from the left. Nehuen Perez rose highest in the box, powering a header into the net from close range to give his side an early lead. As the first half progressed, the drama intensified. Deniz Gul thought he had doubled the lead in the 34th minute, but the celebrations were cut short. After a lengthy VAR review, the referee ruled the goal out for offside, a decision that kept Rio Ave within touching distance despite FC Porto 's superior ball possession and pressure. Substitutions and a Late Twist Both managers turned to their benches in the second half to break the deadlock of the midfield battle. FC Porto introduced In-Beom Hwang and Borja Sainz in the 66th minute, a move that would eventually define the closing stages. Rio Ave responded with their own tactical shifts, pushing higher up the pitch to test the visitors' defensive resolve. In the 82nd minute, the substitutes combined to stunning effect. In-Beom Hwang provided a brilliant assist for Borja Sainz , who struck a clinical right-footed shot into the goal to level the score. In a frantic final period, Stephen Eustaquio nearly snatched a winner for the visitors, but his goalbound effort was saved, ensuring both teams left with a hard-earned point."
